# Converge (Plan ↔ Code Gap Check)

Verify that every requirement, referenced file, and invariant in the approved plan has actually converged in code—consulting `{{index .ResourcePaths "rule/engineering"}}` and project constitution rules (`.dtkit/constitution.md` or `docs/code-standards.md`).

## When to use
- Right after implementing phases (`{{index .SkillNames "implement"}}`) and before final review (`{{index .SkillNames "review"}}`).
- When resuming an unfinished multi-phase implementation to see what remains.

## When not to use
- Requirements have not been planned yet (`{{index .SkillNames "plan"}}`).

## Steps
1. Run `dtkit converge --json` (or MCP `dtkit_converge`) to inspect open `- [ ]` checklist items, missing plan-referenced files, and `dtkit guard verify` receipt status.
2. Read the project constitution (`.dtkit/constitution.md` or `docs/code-standards.md` when present); classify any `MUST`/`NEVER` violation as **CRITICAL**.
3. Report gaps using `{{index .ResourcePaths "template/convergence-report"}}`.
4. Only when remaining items exist and the user requests updating a task tracker, run `dtkit converge --append-tasks <file> --yes` (append-only, never deleting history); when converged, leave files untouched.

## Constraints
- **Strictly read-only verification:** Do not edit application code or rewrite existing plan/spec files during `converge`; hand missing work back to `{{index .SkillNames "implement"}}`.
- **Non-negotiable constitution authority:** Never dilute or bypass a constitution rule to mark work converged.
- **No fabricated verification:** Require a passing `dtkit guard verify` receipt before reporting `converged`.

## Examples
1. **Pre-review check:** Run `dtkit converge` after Phase 3 -> catches one unimplemented test file referenced in the plan before entering `review`.
2. **Clean convergence:** All checklist items checked, all files present, `dtkit guard verify` passes -> outputs `converged` with zero edits.
